---
description: JStack per-role model choices (overrides skill defaults)
alwaysApply: true
---
# JStack model configuration. One line per role. Delete a line to fall back to the skill default.
# `inherit-parent` or `auto` as a value: the role runs on the parent chat model (omit Task `model`). Alias entries in a panel list still count toward its fan-out.
# budget: per role (Opus at high by default, extra high only where deeper reasoning changes the outcome)
# JStack: James Woods's choices, picked by CursorBench and Artificial Analysis scores. Anthropic leads every role; no OpenAI models.
# Gemini appears only as a second seat on panels an Anthropic agent leads; it never owns a task on its own.
# Each line is already matched to its job: use the level as written and don't lower it. Raise one step only for the hardest or subtlest work.
# Code delegates (feature, refactoring, bug-fix, perf-issue, hillclimb) start on Opus 5.5 Medium. Pick claude-opus-5-5-high for a very complex change, claude-sonnet-5-5-high for very well-planned work, or claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh for a simple change with some ambiguity.
# Never start an Anthropic model on max. Escalating to max for the hardest or subtlest work, as j-mode allows, is fine.
feature, refactoring: claude-opus-5-5-medium
bug-fix: claude-opus-5-5-medium
perf-issue: claude-opus-5-5-medium
hillclimb: claude-opus-5-5-medium
judgment and prose: claude-opus-5-5-high
hardest tasks: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
how explorer: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
how explainer: claude-opus-5-5-high
why investigators: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
why synthesizer: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
reflect tooling: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
arena runners: claude-opus-5-5-high, gemini-4-argon-high
arena cross-judge pool: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
swarm workers: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
architect runners: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh, gemini-4-argon-high
interrogate reviewers: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh, gemini-4-argon-high
